# Copy this file to .env (development) and fill in real values. Never commit .env itself -
# it's already covered by .gitignore. Production secrets belong in the hosting platform's
# environment/secret manager, never in a committed file (section 25).

# --- Database (Phase 14) ---------------------------------------------------
# Local dev Postgres (see prisma/schema.prisma). Format:
# postgresql://<user>:<password>@<host>:<port>/<database>?schema=public
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres:CHANGE_ME@127.0.0.1:5432/b2b_procurement?schema=public"

# --- Auth --------------------------------------------------------------
# Random 32+ byte secret used to sign/verify session-related tokens. Generate with:
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
AUTH_SECRET="CHANGE_ME"

# Session cookie lifetime, in seconds. 7 days by default.
SESSION_TTL_SECONDS=604800

# --- Environment ---------------------------------------------------------
# development | test | staging | production
NODE_ENV="development"

# --- Mobile money gateways (section 26's provider abstraction) --------------
# Real values are never committed. Each of the three networks needs all three of
# _SUBSCRIPTION_KEY/_API_USER/_API_KEY before its provider (server/services/payment/gateways/
# mobileMoneyProvider.ts) will attempt a real HTTP charge - missing any one of them, that
# network falls back to an instant-success simulation instead (so the app stays usable without a
# merchant agreement). A charge against a real gateway is asynchronous - it comes back PENDING,
# not PAID, until the customer approves the prompt on their phone and either a webhook
# (POST /api/webhooks/payments/[provider]) or the reconciliation job below confirms it.
#
# MTN MoMo's Collections API is publicly documented at momodeveloper.mtn.com - sign up there for
# a free sandbox subscriptionKey/apiUser/apiKey; the base URL default below already points at
# MTN's own sandbox. Telecel Cash and AirtelTigo Money have no equivalent public developer
# portal - get real values (and confirm the actual base URL/endpoint paths, which this repo has
# NOT verified for these two networks the way it has for MTN) from that network's own
# integration team or a licensed aggregator (Hubtel, ExpressPay, Paystack, ...).
MTN_MOMO_BASE_URL="https://sandbox.momodeveloper.mtn.com"
MTN_MOMO_SUBSCRIPTION_KEY=""
MTN_MOMO_API_USER=""
MTN_MOMO_API_KEY=""
MTN_MOMO_TARGET_ENVIRONMENT="sandbox"

TELECEL_CASH_BASE_URL=""
TELECEL_CASH_SUBSCRIPTION_KEY=""
TELECEL_CASH_API_USER=""
TELECEL_CASH_API_KEY=""
TELECEL_CASH_TARGET_ENVIRONMENT="sandbox"

AIRTELTIGO_MONEY_BASE_URL=""
AIRTELTIGO_MONEY_SUBSCRIPTION_KEY=""
AIRTELTIGO_MONEY_API_USER=""
AIRTELTIGO_MONEY_API_KEY=""
AIRTELTIGO_MONEY_TARGET_ENVIRONMENT="sandbox"

# HMAC-SHA256 secret for verifying inbound payment webhooks (Phase 14, Stage 11 - section 20's
# "verify webhook signatures" rule). Generate with:
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
# Every request to POST /api/webhooks/payments/[provider] is rejected while this is empty - it's
# optional only in the sense that nothing currently sends real webhooks yet.
PAYMENT_WEBHOOK_SIGNING_SECRET=""

# --- Background jobs (deployment-readiness follow-up to section 16) ---------
# Shared secret an external scheduler sends on every /api/cron/* request - as the `x-cron-secret`
# header (system crontab + curl, a GitHub Actions workflow - anything that can send an arbitrary
# header), OR as `Authorization: Bearer <CRON_SECRET>` (Phase 23 - the ONLY header Vercel Cron
# itself sends automatically; Vercel adds this header on its own whenever a project env var
# literally named CRON_SECRET is set, and vercel.json's cron config has no field to customize the
# header it sends). Every cron route also responds to GET as well as POST (Phase 23 - Vercel Cron
# always invokes its configured path with GET, never POST). Generate the secret the same way as
# the webhook secret above. Every cron route is rejected while this is empty. See vercel.json
# (this repo) for the exact schedules if deploying to Vercel, or point any other scheduler at:
#   /api/cron/invoice-due-sweep       - hourly or so; flips PENDING invoices past their due
#                                       date to OVERDUE and notifies the billed company.
#   /api/cron/low-stock-sweep         - hourly or so; notifies each supplier's admins once
#                                       per product per 24h while stock is at or below threshold.
#   /api/cron/pending-payment-sweep   - every few minutes; reconciles mobile money payments
#                                       still PENDING because a webhook never arrived. Only
#                                       does anything once a real gateway above is configured.
#   /api/cron/recurring-purchase-sweep - hourly or so; executes any due recurring purchase
#                                        schedule and advances it to its next occurrence.
CRON_SECRET=""

# --- Object storage (Phase 20/21) --------------------------------------------
# RFQ/purchase-request document uploads (server/services/documents.service.ts) work today with no
# configuration at all - they use LocalDiskStorageProvider (server/services/storage/), which
# writes to a .uploads/ directory on the running instance's own disk. That's fine for local
# development or a genuinely single-instance deployment, but unsuitable once more than one
# instance runs (each instance would see a different, incomplete set of files) - see
# DEPLOYMENT.md's Object Storage section.
#
# Setting ALL FOUR of the variables below switches storage/index.ts over to S3StorageProvider - a
# real S3-compatible client (server/services/storage/s3Storage.ts, @aws-sdk/client-s3) that works
# against real AWS S3 (leave STORAGE_ENDPOINT unset) or any S3-compatible provider (Cloudflare R2,
# DigitalOcean Spaces, MinIO, Backblaze B2, ...) by setting STORAGE_ENDPOINT to that provider's
# endpoint URL. No bucket or credentials are provided by this repo - this has been verified with
# the real S3 SDK's commands mocked (s3Storage.test.ts), never against a real bucket. Leaving any
# of the four unset keeps LocalDiskStorageProvider active.
STORAGE_BUCKET=""
STORAGE_REGION=""
STORAGE_ACCESS_KEY_ID=""
STORAGE_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=""
# Only needed for a non-AWS S3-compatible provider - leave unset for real AWS S3.
STORAGE_ENDPOINT=""

# --- Redis / background jobs (section 16 - future stage) --------------------
REDIS_URL=""

# --- Content Security Policy (Phase 17) --------------------------------------
# CSP is enforced by default - src/proxy.ts mints a fresh nonce every request and sets a real,
# blocking Content-Security-Policy header, live-verified across every workspace with zero
# violations (see PHASE17_FINAL_REPORT.md). Set to "false" only as an emergency rollback to
# Report-Only (never blocks, just logs to /api/csp-report) without a redeploy, if real production
# traffic surfaces an inline script this session's manual verification didn't happen to exercise.
CSP_ENFORCED=""
